Records allow customization within boundaries. You can add **static fields and methods**, **instance methods**, and **override** any generated method. You can also add **constructors** — but every constructor must delegate to the canonical constructor.

The **compact constructor** is the recommended customization point for validation and normalization. It has no parameter list — the parameters are implicit, and the field assignments happen automatically after the body executes.

```java
